course: dictionary
lesson: 1311
title: One word, many jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. This is called using context. The word caddy is a good example, because it can name a person, a box, or a holder.
explain: «Before stacking plates, scrape the leftovers into the bin or the food caddy, a small bin just for food scraps.» The words after the comma tell you what a food caddy is: a small bin just for food scraps. The clues are plates, leftovers and stacking, so this caddy is in the kitchen.
explain: Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense. If a sentence says «She caddied for her dad at golf», the -ied ending tells you caddy is being used as a doing word.
fact: A caddy is a small box, tin or holder that keeps things tidy, such as a pencil caddy or a shower caddy.
fact: A tea caddy is a small box or tin for keeping tea leaves.
fact: A food caddy is a small bin just for food scraps, used in the kitchen in the UK.
fact: A caddy (also spelled caddie) is a person who carries a golfer's clubs and gives advice during a game.
fact: To caddy means to work as a golfer's caddy. Caddy can be a noun (a thing or a person) or a verb (a doing word).
exercise: In golf, what is a caddy? | A tin for keeping tea leaves | *A person who carries a golfer's clubs and gives advice | A cup used in the kitchen
exercise: «She keeps her pencils tidy in a pencil caddy on the desk.» What is a pencil caddy? | *A small holder that keeps pencils tidy | A ruler for drawing straight lines | A pencil that writes in blue
exercise: «She caddied for her dad at the golf club.» What does caddied mean here? | Painted the fence at home | *Worked as a golfer's caddy, carrying the clubs | Cooked a meal for the family
test: «He asked the caddy for a driver.» Who is the caddy in this sentence? | *A golfer's helper who carries the clubs | A tin for tea | A bin for scraps
test: Which of these is a shower caddy? | A bathtub for two people | *A small holder that keeps soap and shampoo tidy | A towel rail on the wall
exam: Which sentence uses caddy as a verb? | *«She caddied for her dad at the golf club.» | The food caddy is full of scraps | The tea caddy is on the shelf
